\section{Introduction}
Beeke (Beke, Ibeeke; ISO 639-3 \texttt{bkf}) is a Bantu language of the Democratic Republic of the Congo with fewer than about 1,000 speakers, reportedly giving way to Ndaka. Its classification is uncertain (possibly a divergent form of Bali). Only descriptive overviews were found.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
None found.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia overview: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beeke_language}
\item Verbix endangered-language page: \url{https://docs.verbix.com/EndangeredLanguages/Beeke}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Joshua Project people-group page (relies on unnamed internal baselines; treat with caution): \url{https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/10760}
\end{itemize}

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Endangered Languages Project entry: \url{https://endangeredlanguages.com/lang/584}
\end{itemize}

